\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces  ExaHyPE~2's Finite Volume scheme organises its mesh into patches. Here, we use a 5$\times $5 patch (orange/red). Prior to the update of a patch, ExaHyPE~2\ calls \texttt  {boundaryConditions} for each of the volumes adjacent to the boundary (darker red). The routine allows you to alter the value of the halo surrounding the patch (blue). The outer (blue) cells are subsequentially used to determine a flow through the boundary into the domain.  }}{31}{figure.4.2}}
\newlabel{figure:exahype:boundary-conditions}{{4.2}{31}{\ExaHyPE 's Finite Volume scheme organises its mesh into patches. Here, we use a 5$\times $5 patch (orange/red). Prior to the update of a patch, \ExaHyPE \ calls \texttt {boundaryConditions} for each of the volumes adjacent to the boundary (darker red). The routine allows you to alter the value of the halo surrounding the patch (blue). The outer (blue) cells are subsequentially used to determine a flow through the boundary into the domain}{figure.4.2}{}}
